# Every text file in this repo uses LF, on every machine. Without this, git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks
# files out with CRLF, and the scripts that read Markdown (handoff, setup-check, after-lesson, make-lesson) miss
# headings and blocks they look for with "\n". The scripts also accept CRLF now; this keeps the files clean anyway.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
